z_order:

```rust
fn z_order(&self, x_: f64, y_: f64) -> i32 {
    let mut x = ((x_ - self.min_x) * self.inv_size) as i32;
    let mut y = ((y_ - self.min_y) * self.inv_size) as i32;
    x = (x | (x << 8)) & 0x00FF00FF;
    x = (x | (x << 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
    x = (x | (x << 2)) & 0x33333333;
    x = (x | (x << 1)) & 0x55555555;
    y = (y | (y << 8)) & 0x00FF00FF;
    y = (y | (y << 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
    y = (y | (y << 2)) & 0x33333333;
    y = (y | (y << 1)) & 0x55555555;
    x | (y << 1)
}
```

C++ `static_cast<int32_t>(double)` truncates toward zero; Rust `as i32` also truncates (and saturates for out-of-range/NaN — C++ would be UB but values are in range). Values: (x_-minX)*inv_size ∈ [0, 32767.5] → fits.

